    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="0827" n="813" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.51/7–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-24T18:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>607. For confidential info of Emb, Board of Trustees of Eximbank considered
                    request of Corporacion de Fomento for financial assistance for construction of
                    the steel mill. Chairman of the Board,<anchor n="60" xml:id="d660-f1"/> at
                    suggestion of Dept of Commerce, requested that decision on this project be
                    deferred until subsequent meeting of Board without prejudice to project.</p>
                <p>Sec of Commerce<anchor n="61" xml:id="d660-f2"/> indicated he would be better
                    satisfied if Chileans would make up comprehensive plan for economic expansion
                    and would determine their overall need for foreign credit instead of making
                    piecemeal approach. As result Bank will again request Chileans to prepare such a
                    plan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
